---
import {
  AiChat02Icon,
  Analytics01Icon,
  ChartLineData01Icon,
  Route01Icon,
} from '@hugeicons/core-free-icons'
import FeaturePage from '@/components/FeaturePage.astro'

const related = [
  { title: 'seo report', text: 'The ai-queries section and visits from AI assistants in the overview.', href: '/docs/report', icon: Analytics01Icon },
  { title: 'Analytics', text: 'Connect Google Analytics or Clicky.', href: '/docs/analytics', icon: ChartLineData01Icon },
  { title: 'seo crawl', text: 'What AI crawlers can read on your site.', href: '/docs/crawl', icon: Route01Icon },
  { title: 'seo compare', text: 'AI visits before and after a change.', href: '/docs/compare', icon: AiChat02Icon },
]
---

<FeaturePage
  title="AI search tracking from your own data"
  description="See how AI search reaches your site: the questions people ask Google AI Mode and AI assistants that show in Search Console, visits from ChatGPT and Perplexity, and what AI crawlers can read."
  path="/features/ai-search"
  lead="See the questions people ask AI about your topic, the visits AI assistants send you, and what AI crawlers can read, all from your own Search Console, analytics and site."
  {related}
>
  <h2>The questions people ask AI</h2>
  <p>
    When people use Google's AI Mode, and when AI assistants search the web
    for them, their questions show up in your Search Console. They look
    different from normal searches:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>Bare replies, such as "yes" or "tell me more".</li>
    <li>Follow-ups, such as "what about smith" or "is it common".</li>
    <li>Long, chat-style questions in full sentences.</li>
    <li>Agent searches, such as a question with <code>site:</code> added, or a whole prompt.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Your agent finds these queries, groups the many rewordings of one
    question, and shows the page Google picked for each, with impressions,
    clicks and position. These are real questions from your own data, not a
    list of prompts someone guessed.
  </p>

  <h2>Visits from AI assistants</h2>
  <p>
    From Google Analytics, your agent sees the visits that ChatGPT,
    Perplexity, Claude, Gemini and Copilot send you, by source, and the pages
    they land on, against the previous period.
  </p>

  <h2>What AI crawlers can read</h2>
  <p>
    A crawl of your site shows which AI search and training bots your
    robots.txt allows, whether your pages have Markdown copies, and whether
    your llms.txt and its links work. See the <a href="/features/seo-audit">SEO
    audit tool</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Read it as a signal</h2>
  <p>
    Search Console does not label AI Mode, so the questions are found by
    their shape, and some will have been typed by people. Search Console also
    leaves out rare queries, so the counts are a minimum. Visits only count
    when the AI app passes a referrer.
  </p>
</FeaturePage>
